 **Upgrading from v0.3.0-beta.1:** stop the Relic App's server first (its process id is `pid` in `~/.relic/app.json`), then extract the new package and run its installer. Organizations carry over. Run `/reload-plugins` in Claude Code sessions that are already open, and restart Codex, which loads the plugin version it has cached when it starts. See the [upgrade notes](docs/guide.en.md#9-storage-updates-and-removal).
 
-**macOS status: not released.** Existing CI results are development evidence, not real Mac desktop acceptance. macOS downloads are withheld until testing on a Mac is complete. See the [development draft](docs/macos.en.md).
+### macOS Apple silicon beta
+
+Download [`relic-macos-v0.4.1-macos-beta.1.zip`](https://github.com/Hongyi-Du/Relic-Plugins/releases/download/v0.4.1-macos-beta.1/relic-macos-v0.4.1-macos-beta.1.zip) from the [Mac prerelease](https://github.com/Hongyi-Du/Relic-Plugins/releases/tag/v0.4.1-macos-beta.1), extract it to a permanent folder, then run:
+
+```bash
+bash install.command --host none --open
+```
+
+Requires native **arm64 Python 3.11+**, **Node.js 22+ with npm**, and installed, signed-in Claude Code and/or Codex. The installer creates `~/Applications/Relic.app`; keep the extracted folder in place. `--host none` installs the App alone; use `--host both` to also register the CLI plugins. Install the App's adapters in Settings → Harness connections before running members.
+
+This prerelease supports **Apple silicon only** and uses the older **v0.4.1** baseline. Its source and instructions are at the [Mac release tag](https://github.com/Hongyi-Du/Relic-Plugins/tree/v0.4.1-macos-beta.1) and [Mac installation guide](https://github.com/Hongyi-Du/Relic-Plugins/blob/v0.4.1-macos-beta.1/docs/macos.en.md); the main branch continues to describe Windows v0.6.0-beta.1.
 
